@startuml
title MEDORA: Standard Outpatient Patient Journey
!include ../../../shared/templates/medora-style.puml
skinparam dpi 192
skinparam defaultFontSize 16
skinparam wrapWidth 130
skinparam maxMessageSize 130
|Receptionist|
start
:Identify patient and search for an existing record;
if (Existing record found?) then (yes)
  :Confirm permitted demographic details;
else (no)
  :Register patient after duplicate warning review;
endif
if (Appointment exists?) then (yes)
  :Check in the booked appointment;
else (no)
  :Register walk-in under facility policy;
endif
:Create or activate Encounter and assign queue;
|Nurse|
:Record screening and vital signs;
|Doctor|
:Review permitted longitudinal information;
:Document consultation, symptoms and diagnosis;
if (Prescription or service order required?) then (yes)
  :Issue prescription and/or create and schedule service order;
else (no)
  :Continue without a new prescription or service order;
endif
if (Service order created?) then (yes)
  |Technician / Service Staff|
  :Perform service and record result or status;
  |Doctor|
  :Review result when required for the care plan;
else (no)
endif
:Complete encounter summary and follow-up plan;
|Cashier|
:Create invoice from eligible items;
:Record payment or outstanding status;
stop

note right
  Business workflow, not a use-case specification.
  Each clinical or financial action remains subject to
  role, scope and state validation.
end note
@enduml
